      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "χMT = 31.75 cm3·K·mol−1 at room temperature is nearly constant to 53 K, then falls to 10.49 cm3·K·mol−1 at 2.0 K, indicating antiferromagnetic Gd···Gd coupling. PHI fit of H = −2J1 SGd1SGd2 − 2J2 SGd1SGd1A − 2J3 SGd1ASGd2A gives g = 2.0, J1 = J3 = −0.139 cm−1, J2 = −0.075 cm−1. Magnetization at 2.0 K is 27.34 Nβ at 70 kOe, near the 28 Nβ saturation expected for four isolated Gd3+ ions.",
